/-
OEIS A187011: a(n) = det(|p_i - p_j|)_{1 ≤ i,j ≤ n}, p_k the k-th prime
(offset 0, a(0) = 1).  Conjecture (Zhi-Wei Sun, entry text):
(-1)^(n-1) a(n) > 0 for all n > 1, and |a(n)|^(1/n) tends to infinity.
Both halves are checked here.  Generated by
OEIS/A187011/certificate/assemble.py; edit the parts, not this file.

Checked here (Lean 4.35.0, Mathlib 56a00585):
* `A187011_formula`: for n ≥ 2, a n = (-1)^(n-1) 2^(n-2) (p (n-1) - p 0)
  ∏_{i<n-1} (p (i+1) - p i), with p i = Nat.nth Nat.Prime i (p 0 = 2).
* `A187011_sign`: 2 ≤ n → 0 < (-1)^(n-1) a n.
* `A187011_growth`: Tendsto (fun n => |(a n : ℝ)| ^ (1 / n)) atTop atTop.
* `A187011_conjecture`: the conjunction of the two halves.
Ingredients of the growth half: `smallGap_card_le` (gaps ≤ H among the first
m give prime pairs q, q + h below p m), the uniform Selberg bound
`pairCount_le_log` for prime pairs, and Chebyshev's lower bound
`Chebyshev.pi_ge` from Mathlib.

Not checked here: nothing the statements depend on.  The identification of
`a n` with the OEIS data is by definition (determinant of the distance
matrix of the first n primes); OEIS/A187011/certificate/check.py compares
the closed form with the data terms numerically.

Layout: (1) FAM/twin-primes/twin_primes_mathlib.lean, which starts with a
verbatim copy (edits listed in FAM/twin-primes/certificate/assemble.py) of
the Selberg sieve files of PrimeNumberTheoremAnd
(Mathlib/NumberTheory/Sieve/{AuxResults,Basic,Selberg,SelbergBounds}.lean,
commit 127b50e3, Apache 2.0, author Arend Mellendijk), inlined because the
checker accepts one file; (2) OEIS/A187011/A187011_mathlib.lean;
(3) OEIS/A187011/certificate/Growth.lean.part.
-/
